1. Backend Migration to PostgreSQL
   - Status: Completed
   - Notes: Migration finished and verified in production.

2. Frontend Redesign
   - Status: In progress (80% complete)
   - Notes: Remaining work focuses on responsive behaviors and final UI polish.

3. Notification Module (QA Testing)
   - Status: Delayed
   - Cause: Missing test cases prevented QA from completing verification.
   - Impact: Could delay notification-related releases if not resolved.
   - Mitigation: Engineering and QA are collaborating to produce missing test cases; testing will resume 
immediately after.

4. API Documentation
   - Status: Finalized
   - Notes: Documentation is complete and available internally.

5. Internal Dashboard
   - Status: Deployed for stakeholder review
   - Notes: Collecting feedback; prioritizing any critical items.

Risks & Mitigations:
- QA test-case gap is the primary risk; engineering and QA are prioritizing remediation.
- Monitor frontend completion to avoid blocking upcoming releases.
- Address stakeholder feedback on the dashboard promptly to keep momentum.

Next Steps:
- QA: finalize missing test cases and complete notification module testing.
- Frontend: complete remaining redesign tasks and validate across supported platforms.
- Dashboard: incorporate stakeholder feedback and schedule follow-up review.
- Operations: continue monitoring production systems after the DB migration.

